<title>POLAND: All Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</title>
<headline>All Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish T-bills fell at today's primary auction on total demand of 738 million zlotys against a 1.2 million zloty offer, the National Bank of Poland said.</p>
<p>The finance ministry sold 617 million zlotys of its bills.  </p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week 52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    ---     94.84    90.18     ---     82.14</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (94.90)  (90.23)    ---    (82.25)</p>
<p>   new max price    ---     95.30    90.40     ---     82.35</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (95.10)  (90.46)    ---    (82.41)</p>
<p>   offer		---     400.0    200.0     ---     600.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    ---     214.8     64.6     ---     458.9</p>
<p>   bids accepted    ---     201.5     51.1     ---     365.9</p>
<p>   next auction     ---     200.0    200.0     ---     600.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
